+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time into a
+{class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number of seconds,
+like `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d`
+(days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds), like `2d`, `1h30m`, or
+`1d2h3m4s`. Each unit may appear at most once and in that order, with no
+spaces. Units are case-insensitive. A `timedelta` value, like a default, is
+passed through unchanged.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting for {timeout}")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=30m1h'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
